        "problem": "There is a pair of prime numbers whose difference is $2.$\n\nExpress the statement above in formal language.",
        "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The words \"there is\" indicate that we use an existential quantifier, $\u2203.$\n\n- The sentence refers to two prime numbers. So, by denoting our numbers as $p$ and $q,$ we have\n\n$$\n\u2203\\,p,q\\text{\u00a0primes}.\n$$\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as follows:\n\n$$\np-q=2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows:\n\n$\u2203\\,p,q$ primes, $p-q=2$",
